+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are the `apiKeys`
+in the data file (`docs/DATA.md`); each has a role:
+
+- `viewer`: every `GET` route except `GET /audit`.
+- `cook`: the same, plus `POST /recipes/:id/cook`,
+  `POST /batches/:id/waste`, `POST /temperatures` and
+  `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: every route, including `GET /audit`.
+
+A request without a key or with an unknown key gets 401 `unauthorized`
+(whatever the path); a known key whose role does not allow the route gets
+403 `forbidden`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request with a known key that is not a `GET` writes an audit entry,
+whether it succeeded or not (a refused or failed attempt is recorded with its
+status). `GET /audit` (managers only) lists them newest first:
+
+    { "id": 7, "at": "2026-10-28T10:00:00.000Z", "keyName": "seed cook",
+      "method": "POST", "path": "/recipes/1/cook", "status": 200 }
+
+Requests answered 401 are not recorded: there is no key name to record.
+
